===============================================================================
3. Third-party material
===============================================================================

The licences above cover the author's own work. Some data files are derived
from published sources, which must be credited when the files are reused:

* data/bsc_outbreaks/tables/park2020_callcentre_seats_digitized.csv and
  park2020_callcentre_epicurve_digitized.csv: digitised from Figs 1 and 2 of
  Park et al., Emerging Infectious Diseases 26(8), 2020,
  doi:10.3201/eid2608.201274.
* data/bsc_outbreaks/tables/hu2021_train_attack_matrix.csv: transcribed from
  Hu et al., Clinical Infectious Diseases 72(4), 2021,
  doi:10.1093/cid/ciaa1057.
* data/bsc_outbreaks/tables/li2021_restaurant_tables.csv: transcribed from
  Li et al., Building and Environment 196, 2021,
  doi:10.1016/j.buildenv.2021.107788, and Lu et al., Emerging Infectious
  Diseases 26(7), 2020, doi:10.3201/eid2607.200764.
* data/bsc_outbreaks/outbreaks.csv and outbreaks.json: numbers transcribed
  from the 31 sources listed in data/bsc_outbreaks/sources.md.

No source text or figure of a third party is included in this repository.

===============================================================================
4. Third-party data
===============================================================================

data/schools/matsumoto_students.csv is a tabular copy of data published by
A. Endo and co-authors (github.com/akira-endo/schooldynamics_FluMatsumoto14-15)
under the MIT License, Copyright (c) 2020 Akira Endo; the licence text is in
data/schools/LICENSE_matsumoto.txt.

data/tracer/kinahan_*.csv are extracts of the workbooks published by
S. M. Kinahan and co-authors on figshare (doi:10.6084/m9.figshare.13537349.v1
and doi:10.6084/m9.figshare.13537319.v1) under CC BY 4.0.

The outbreak records, seat maps and the other tracer tables are numbers
transcribed or digitised from the publications listed in the SOURCES.md and
sources.md files next to them. The SocioPatterns contact records are not
redistributed (see data/contacts/SOURCES.md).
